Marquee changes (each changed spot carries a "Marquee fork" comment), from the
engine review of 2026-10-20 (plans/reviews/engine-2026-10-20-r1.md,
P1-1):

- src/deserialize.rs: `MAX_DEPTH` (32) and `Error::TooDeep`. The deserializer
  counts the lists and dicts open around its position and refuses one more
  past the bound before it recurses. Every parse goes through it: tracker
  announce and scrape answers, DHT messages, peer extended messages and
  ut_metadata, torrent files. Unbounded, 10,000 nested lists overflowed a
  2 MiB thread stack and aborted the process.
- src/lib.rs: exports `MAX_DEPTH`.
